The standard fflib pattern: the domain class declares `public class Constructor implements fflib_SObjectDomain.IConstructable`. And fflib's `construct` method:

```apex
public static fflib_SObjectDomain construct(Type domainClass, List<SObject> sObjectList)
{
    fflib_SObjectDomain domain = null;
    Type constructableType = Type.forName(domainClass.getName() + '.Constructor');
    if(constructableType != null)
    {
        fflib_SObjectDomain.IConstructable constructable = (fflib_SObjectDomain.IConstructable) constructableType.newInstance();
        domain = constructable.construct(sObjectList);
    }
    else
    {
        // fallback to default constructor
    }
    return domain;
}
```

